.he "gtty (3)                     10/28/26                     gtty (3)"
.fo "                               -#-"
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
SUBROUTINE
.in +5
.br
.bd
gtty
- get typewriter status
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
C
.in +5
.br
.bd
#include <sys/sgtty.h>
.sp
.nf
.bd 3
gtty(descriptor, vec)
int descriptor;
struct sgtty *vec;
.fi
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
FUNCTION
.in +5
.br
.bd
Gtty
asks the character device named by
.bd
descriptor
for its status and writes the six-byte
.bd
struct sgtty
pointed at by
.bd
vec:
.sp
.in +4
.nf
.bd 5
char	ispeed;		/* input speed */
char	ospeed;		/* output speed */
char	erase;		/* erase character */
char	kill;		/* kill character */
UINT	mode;		/* see below */
.in -4
.fi
.sp
It is the request
.bd
TIOCGETA
through
.bd
ioctl
(2), so it may be made to any character device;
a device with no terminal status answers ENOTTY.
.bd
Stty
(3) is the other half and sets the same block.

.bd
Ispeed
and
.bd
ospeed
are one of:
.nf
.in +4
.bd 16
0     1200 baud
1       50 baud
2       75 baud
3      110 baud
4      134.5 baud
5      150 baud
6      200 baud
7      300 baud
8      600 baud
9     1200 baud
10    1800 baud
11    2400 baud
12    4800 baud
13    9600 baud
14   19200 baud
15    1200 baud
.in -4
.fi
.bp
The next two characters are the erase and
kill characters.  The defaults are ^H and ^X.
.sp
The mode says what the system does to input and output.
Currently these bits are defined:
.nf
.in +4
.bd 6
0100000  use the RS-232 clear-to-send line
 040000  keep all 8 bits of input
   0040  raw input
   0020  cr -> lf mapping
   0010  echo input
   0002  expand tabs
.in -4
.fi
.sp
In raw mode every character goes straight to the program
without waiting for a line, there is no erase or kill
processing, and no control character is recognised.
In cooked mode the following are recognised:
.in +4
.nf
.bd 6
^D  end-of-file, alone on a line
^\  quit signal to the tty's processes
DEL interrupt signal to the same
^B  background signal to the same
ESC freeze output from this tty
^S  same as ESC
.in -4
.fi
.sp
Even in raw mode the other mode bits still apply.  With
cr->lf mapping, input crs become lfs and output crs or lfs
become cr-lfs.  With echo, input is echoed as it is typed;
raw echoes it exactly, cooked does not echo the special
characters, echoes kill as itself and a newline, and echoes
erase as backspace-space-backspace.  With tab expansion,
tabs go out as the spaces needed to reach the next column
that is a multiple of eight.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
RETURNS
.in +5
.br
0 on success, with the status in the structure; -1 on failure.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
ERRORS
.in +5
.br
.bd
EBADF
if descriptor is not an open file.
.br
.bd
ENOTTY
if it does not name a character device, or the device has no
terminal status.
